videos.script:
The planner has a version in four files, and today they say three different things. {{four}}

A phone wants two numbers: one for people, and one for the store, which may only ever grow. {{two}}

So the version gets one home, package.json, and a small script copies it everywhere else. One command then moves all four files and tags the release. {{bump}}

Then the desktop app learns to update itself. An old version is installed, a new one is served, and you watch the old one find it, fetch it and replace itself. {{update}} And when one byte of the new file is changed, it refuses. {{refused}}

Last, the phones, where the store is the updater, and you only choose how fast a release reaches people. {{rollout}}
